<article class="env-lemma" id="0GD1">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GD1">Lemma <span data-tag="0GD1">88.20.5</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ and $g : Z \to Y$ be morphisms of locally Noetherian formal algebraic spaces over $S$. If $f$ is rig-étale and $g$ is adic, then the base change $X \times _ Y Z \to Z$ is rig-étale. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Formal Spaces, Remark <a href="/tag/0GBG" data-tag="0GBG">87.21.10</a> and the discussion in Formal Spaces, Section <a href="/tag/0AQ2" data-tag="0AQ2">87.23</a>, this follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/0GCW" data-tag="0GCW">88.19.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>